WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.515
The CPU handles general computation, application logic, tokenization,

00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:06.746
and inference when no accelerator is used.

00:00:06.746 --> 00:00:09.780
CPU inference can be useful for smaller or highly quantized models,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.584
but memory bandwidth and core behavior influence performance.

00:00:12.584 --> 00:00:17.480
A GPU provides parallel compute and high-bandwidth memory suited to model operations.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.345
VRAM is memory on or available to the graphics processor for weights, caches, activations,

00:00:22.345 --> 00:00:23.440
and runtime overhead.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.868
Insufficient VRAM can force offload, reduced settings, or failure.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:31.345
System RAM holds the operating system, runtime, model data, CPU-resident layers, cache,

00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:32.915
and applications.

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:36.030
Unified-memory architectures share a memory pool between CPU and GPU,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.720
reducing some transfers but still operating within total capacity and bandwidth limits.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.860
Storage capacity and speed affect model downloads, startup, swaps, logs, datasets,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.835
and backups.

00:00:45.835 --> 00:00:47.480
Models can consume many gigabytes,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.107
and keeping several formats or quantizations multiplies requirements.

00:00:51.107 --> 00:00:53.610
Preserve enough free space for safe operation and updates.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.019
PCI Express connects discrete devices and can affect transfer behavior when layers or data

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:00.505
move between system memory and GPU memory.

00:01:00.505 --> 00:01:02.520
Power supplies, cooling, chassis airflow,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.840
and electrical capacity determine whether peak performance can be sustained safely.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.000
Laptops trade portability for thermal and power constraints.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.200
Desktops are easier to cool and expand.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.930
Consumer hardware may provide strong value,

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.520
while workstation or server hardware may add memory, reliability, management, and support.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.640
Match the platform to workload and operational expectations.
